# Cursor Rules for Insight Graph Project

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all files
- Use functional components with hooks in React
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow Next.js 14 App Router conventions
- Use server components by default, mark client components explicitly with 'use client'

## Database
- All database queries should use Prisma
- Always set RLS context before queries: `await setRLSContext(userId)`
- Use workspace filtering in all queries
- Optimize with proper indexes

## API Routes
- Always validate with Zod
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Include error handling with Sentry
- Apply rate limiting where appropriate
- Use RLS for data access control

## Components
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract reusable UI to components/ui
- Use shadcn/ui components as base
- Optimize for performance (React.memo, useMemo where needed)

## Performance
- Lazy load heavy components
- Batch LLM calls when possible
- Use React Query for data fetching
- Optimize graph rendering for large datasets

## Security
- Never expose secrets in client code
- Validate all user inputs
- Use RLS policies for multi-tenancy
- Rate limit API endpoints
- Encrypt sensitive data

## Testing
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Write E2E tests for critical flows
- Mock external services in tests
- Test error paths

## Git
- Write clear commit messages
- Keep commits atomic
- Use feature branches
- Run tests before pushing


